cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Resolving fresh groundwater from clay with AEM and surface NMR:
  a staged workflow with a truth firewall
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Neil
    family-names: Symington
    affiliation: Geoscience Australia
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Neil-Symington/snmr-aem-resolvability"
abstract: >-
  A seven-stage workflow that converts an airborne electromagnetic sounding and
  a surface NMR sounding into a verdict on a pre-registered aquifer hypothesis.
  The conductance-to-salinity conversion is clay-free, so the method can certify
  that pore water is fresh but never that it is saline; a saline verdict follows
  only from declared physical ceilings and is labelled as such. No stage after
  the first may read a truth value, and on the synthetic columns that firewall is
  enforced as a file boundary.
keywords:
  - airborne electromagnetics
  - surface nuclear magnetic resonance
  - groundwater salinity
  - trans-dimensional inversion
